The error in the provided implementation is that it attempts to instantiate a module named `not_gate`, but this module has not been defined anywhere in the code. In Verilog, you cannot instantiate a module unless its definition is provided or it is part of a library.

To fix this, you can implement the NOT gate logic directly within the `top_module` using a continuous assignment statement with the bitwise NOT operator (`~`).

```verilog
module top_module(
	input in,
	output out
);

assign out = ~in;

endmodule
```
